// From a Surface to another where the second surface needs Tiled calculations to get at its address.
// Keep in mind, it could be that the first surface is Tiled and the second is pitched. Doesn't matter,
// they are symmetrical, point being you travel in a straight line in one and via jumps like below in the
// other. Which you call pitch and which you call Tiled is upto you ...

void blit(src_addr, p, l, w, h, count) {
   while(count) {
     addr = get_tiled_address(src_addr, p, l, w, h, &offset);
     sx   = offset % w;
     sy   = offset % h;
     for (y = sy; y < h; ++y) {
         for (x = sx; x < w; ++x) {
             *src_addr++ = *addr++; count--; 
             if (!count) return;
         }
         sx = 0; addr += p;
     }
     sy = 0;
   }
}

So you do the gla calculation at Tile boundary. 